        stack: [{ name: "ServiceNow CMDB", role: "IT Asset Data", why: "Configuration items: every system, server, network device, and application. When a student reports 'the system is down,' CMDB tells the agent which system, its current status, and known issues.", href: "/vendors" }, { name: "Canvas / Blackboard", role: "LMS Data", why: "Learning Management System user data and course information. When a student says 'I can't submit my assignment,' the agent needs to see the student's course enrollment, assignment status, and any system errors in the LMS.", href: "/vendors" }],
        pitfall: "LMS issues are the most emotionally charged IT help desk calls, because they affect grades. A student who can't submit an assignment before the deadline due to a technical issue needs both IT resolution AND communication with the instructor. Build a workflow that resolves the technical issue AND generates an automated notification to the instructor documenting the system error and timeline. Without this, the student must persuade the professor that 'the system was down', a claim instructors hear often and cannot check."
